      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This report concerns a 31-year-old woman. It is an intricate case including bilateral self-induced pneumoparotitis, cervical and facial subcutaneous emphysema and limited pneumomediastinum. Besides, this borderline patient simulated asthma attacks. The clinical picture was characteristic of Munchausen's syndrome with multiple hospitalisations in various hospitals, automutilations and intentional production of physical symptoms. The diagnosis and the treatment are discussed."},
